{"name":"Pink Zest","hex":"#f2d8cd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"zest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outer skin of a citrus fruit, used as a flavouring or garnish.","General vibrance of flavour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scrape the zest from a fruit.","To make more zesty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zest (ingredient)","blocks":[{"text":"Zest is a food ingredient that is prepared by scraping or cutting from the rind of unwaxed citrus fruits such as lemon, orange, citron, and lime. Zest is used to add flavor to many different types of food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Zesting_an_orange.jpg/330px-Zesting_an_orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zest_(ingredient)","wikidata":"Q196819"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Juliennejern.JPG/500px-Juliennejern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co